  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "The existing evidence shows a strong RNA-only baseline (scvi_n200 + multiprofile at ~0.65) but the only image-only test (config_010: resnet50, singleprofile) yielded a very weak 0.208 accuracy—essentially at chance level. This creates major uncertainty about whether the image modality contains any useful signal for this task. Config_013 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_010, isolating the effect of a much stronger pretrained image encoder (ViT-L vs ResNet50). If ViT-L substantially improves image-only performance, it justifies investing remaining budget in multimodal fusion experiments. If it remains near chance, it strongly suggests image features are not informative for this task, allowing us to redirect budget toward refining the RNA pipeline (e.g., scgpt+transformer, or singleprofile scvi_n200) rather than exploring 30+ multimodal configurations that would likely underperform the 0.65 RNA baseline. This is the highest-uncertainty-reduction experiment available under the limited budget."
}

